SWEEP FILES (added next to the original vector_add.c / Makefile, which are unchanged)
=====================================================================================
- vadd_sweep.c    - vector add with -DN (size) and -DLMUL (1/2/4/8) flags. Does one
                    warm up pass, then m5 reset_stats / dump_stats around the kernel
                    so the first stats block is the kernel only.
- fir.c           - 16 tap FIR, scalar and RVV, same flags.
- Makefile.sweep  - builds every workload/size/LMUL combo into bin/ (needs clang-18,
                    lld-18 and the riscv64 sysroot, same as the original Makefile).
                      make -f Makefile.sweep          measured binaries
                      make -f Makefile.sweep check    correctness builds (print PASS)
- run_sweep.sh    - runs everything through run_se.py, one output dir per config
                    (results/out_<workload>_N<size>_vlen<vlen>_m<lmul>).
                      ./run_sweep.sh ../build/RISCV/gem5.opt 16 check
                      nohup ./run_sweep.sh ../build/RISCV/gem5.opt 16 > sweep.log 2>&1 &
- parse_stats.py  - results/ -> results.csv (prints the gem5 stat names it reads)
- make_plots.py   - results.csv -> plots/*.png
- findings.txt    - summary of the numbers

NOTE: needs gem5 v26.0. run_se.py does not run on v25.1 (SimpleProcessor has no
      clk_freq argument there).

